Upstream-Name: CoolerControl
Upstream-Contact: Guy Boldon (https://gitlab.com/coolercontrol/coolercontrol)
Source: https://gitlab.com/coolercontrol/coolercontrol
Comment: CoolerControl (the daemon, the interface and the Qt window) is under the GNU General Public License version 3 or later; the
 programming interface's documents and some data files carry the licences REUSE.toml of the project names. The daemon is one Rust
 binary that also links the crates of vendor/ (listed below by the licence each one's Cargo.toml states); the interface is built
 from its own source with the packages of npm (listed below by the licence each one's package.json states), of which only the
 bundler's output is part of the program; Rollup's native part is built from its Rust source and the crates of rollupvendor/. The
 source package carries all of that source and the whole build recipe. The stanzas below are generated
 (sparky-os/packages/coolercontrol/debian/gen-copyright.py in the edition's build repository) from the tables
 debian/crate-licences.tsv, debian/rollup-crate-licences.tsv and debian/npm-licences.tsv, which pin every package's legal files by
 SHA-256; the files themselves (they carry their authors' names and addresses) are not kept in git, build.sh takes them from the
 trees and stops unless each has the pinned hash, and they are installed in /usr/share/doc/coolercontrold/vendor-licences. The
 build stops when this file differs from what the generator gives.

